     LOCATION:    Remote – this is a home based, virtual position. The person in this position is required to maintain residency in North Carolina or within 40 miles of the NC border.           GENERAL STATEMENT OF JOB     The Maternal Health Care Management RN (Maternal Health CM RN) Supervisor reports to the Care Management RN Director. This position provides clinical leadership and direct oversight of Maternal Health CM RN staff and ensures achievement of individual and team performance and productivity standards. The Maternal Health CM RN Supervisor implements process improvement interventions and develops staff in an environment that is motivating. This position promotes effective cross-organization communication and maintains collaborative relationships within the organization to achieve division objectives. The Maternal Health CM RN Supervisor maintains skills in care management, care coordination, disease management and patient transition management to allow for coverage during staffing shortages in the department. Performs other duties as assigned. Work is performed under the supervision of the CM RN Director with clinical oversight provided by the Care Management RN Director, Sr. Director of Integrated Care Management, and the Medical Operations team. This position may work with staff, members and family members as well as community stakeholders. Essential job functions include, but may not be limited to:      Care Management Platform basics    Outreach & Engagement    Release of Information practices    Perinatal Assessment     Medication List and Continuity of Care process    Care Planning in collaboration with the Care Team to include the development of specific, measurable, achievable, relevant, and timebound goals    Member education on maternal/perinatal/postpartum health    Interdisciplinary Care Team and Ongoing Care Management    Direction back to medical provider for medical care and treatment    Referrals to resources to assist member in meeting social driver of health resource needs    Motivational interviewing to assist members in setting health goals and action plans                ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS      Management:        Supervises the Maternal Health CM RN Team by observing and monitoring paperwork/documentation/data/reports to ensure that Care Management RN activities are carried out effectively     Participate in the development and validation of data and reporting projects related to Care Management RN activities     Works in collaboration with Care Management teams and Population Health leadership to identify, develop and implement improvements in member care     Provides coaching to ensure continuous improvement of performance. Conducts trainings on relevant clinical care management topics           Treatment Planning supervision:        Team compliance with Continuity of Care and Care Management Continuum and Vaya Partners policies and procedures. Ensures person-centered principles are utilized by the CM RN and the team in care planning activities for individuals through fidelity reviews or other CM RN quality oversight processes        Provides support to CM RN in addressing barriers to maternal/perinatal/postpartum care for members through convening key providers and others to address needs of the individual or populations at the individual or system level      Proactively works with CM RN team to identify gaps in services and intervenes to ensure that the individuals and specialty populations receive appropriate care     Uses data, chart review and supervision to measure results of intervention and treatment, including reduction in high-risk events and inappropriate service utilization     Ensures that CM RN services for the individual are coordinated across the Vaya Partners system and with other healthcare and social determinant systems    Ensures collaboration with plan and provider-based care managers on care plan development and care plan updates    Escalates high-risk scenarios to appropriate leadership. High-risk can involve Health & Safety of individuals served, staff or organizational risk     Ensures focused attention and more intensive interventions are directed toward members with the highest risk and most complex needs    Understands the role of and collaborates with Care Management and Integrated Health teams re: routine care planning, discharge planning teams, transitional care plans, educating staff and members regarding network services and supports with consideration of medical necessity, funding eligibility and appropriateness of recommendations relative to person centered, recovery principles and known best/appropriate practice     Ensures CM RN Team identifies and communicates gaps in care related to network adequacy to Provider Network Operations for healthcare needs;

Headquarters:  EMEA; Remote Roles - EMEA































  Who We Are  

 At OKX, we believe that the future will be reshaped by crypto, and ultimately contribute to every individual's freedom. 
 OKX is a leading crypto exchange, and the developer of OKX Wallet, giving millions access to crypto trading and decentralized crypto applications (dApps). OKX is also a trusted brand by hundreds of large institutions seeking access to crypto markets. We are safe and reliable, backed by our Proof of Reserves. 
 Across our multiple offices globally, we are united by our core principles:  We Before Me ,  Do the Right Thing , and  Get Things Done . These shared values drive our culture, shape our processes, and foster a friendly, rewarding, and diverse environment for every OK-er. OKX is part of OKG, a group that brings the value of Blockchain to users around the world, through our leading products OKX, OKX Wallet, OKLink and more. 
   

  About the team  
 OKX’s Legal team provides legal advice and guidance to the Company across all coverage areas and geographic locations, and supports business growth and development by working with all teams within the company to help them achieve their goals. We are a high-functioning, collaborative and fast-paced team who enjoys the cutting-edge nature of our work and our industry 






  About the Opportunity  

 You will report to the team’s European Associate General Counsel based in Malta. You will work closely with all members of the Global Legal team and business leaders throughout the company, but will concentrate on supporting OKX's European entities, which are based in Malta. 
 The right candidate will have a basic understanding of and enthusiastic belief in the cryptocurrency/digital asset space, 5+ years of experience working for a top law firm or in-house at a fast-paced, business, and possess strong academic credentials and excellent writing and analytical skills. The ideal candidate should also possess experience working on matters pertaining to cryptocurrency/digital assets, and/or touching upon financial services laws and regulations (for example MICA, GDPR, MIFID). 
 We offer a competitive base salary and bonus structure as well as excellent benefits and an opportunity to work in a cutting-edge industry that will be the future of financial services. 

  What You’ll Be Doing     

 Support the business in virtually all legal coverage areas, including but not limited to complaints and litigation handling, product development, corporate governance, contract negotiation, regulatory matters, compliance legal support, institutional sales and partnerships, and marketing/advertising; 
 Analyze and advise on the legal risk of new and existing digital assets and manage the legal component of the new asset review process; 
 To the extent needed, manage civil or regulatory litigation matters and retain and supervise outside counsel; 
 Manage on-going license obligations, communicating with the Regulator, drafting and maintaining internal policies, and working collaboratively to support the legal function; 
 Collaborate with product and business development teams to achieve company-wide projects and goals; 
 Assist as needed with corporate governance, and other corporate matters; and 
 Manage legal requests from all areas of the business and effectively advise on legal concepts and legal risk with an eye towards the strategic goals of business leaders. 

  What We Look For In You   

 Must possess the academic degree of Doctor of Law (LL.D.) or Master in Advocacy and have obtained the warrant necessary to practice as an Advocate pursuant to the laws of Malta; 
 Resident of Malta; 
 5+ years of experience at a top-tier law firm and/or in-house legal team, preferably in a financial services or crypto industry; 
 Experience advising on cryptocurrency and blockchain technology legal issues (or strong interest and knowledge in the field) and have a basic understanding (or eager to learn) about the relevant legal/regulatory landscape; 
 Comfortable working independently in a fast-paced, growth-stage and multi-cultural environment; 
 Ability to effectively advise and build trust with business teams; 
 Ability to navigate through a rapidly-changing legal landscape and deal with legal ambiguity; 
 Ability to work in a high-functioning legal team and feel comfortable in a collaborative working environment; 
 Self-starter, quick learner who is highly driven, proactive, responsive and precise; 
 Experience working on cross-jurisdictional matters and a global legal team; 
 Drafting, reviewing and negotiating contracts. 

  Perks &  Benefits    


 Competitive total compensation package 


 L&D programs and Education subsidy for employees' growth and development 


 Various team building programs and company events 


 More that we love to tell you along the process!

